      "message": "thanks for the contributions (both on this CL and other similar ones to `git cl`). IMO a feature like this meets the bar for a more thought-out design doc/proposal that considers the overall agentic UX for `git cl`. not to say that this implementation couldn\u0027t be part of that overall effort, but having a detailed plan would be much preferred over ad-hoc CLs like this that shape tooling long-term.\n\nI\u0027ve filed http://b/585157429 on myself to pick up this work (including writing a defined contract/doc) as soon as our team has bandwidth (hopefully in the new few weeks). but for the time being, we\u0027re not likely to accept ad-hoc CLs for agents like this until we\u0027ve thought it out more comprehensively",
